Hi Francois,
Unfortunately subclassification will not work with the Mahalanobis distance (for the same reason that the distance object is filled with NA's).  Subclassification requires each individual to have a single "distance" measure (like the propensity score), in order to create the subclasses.  But the Mahalanobis distance (as implemented in MatchIt) is only relative between two units.  So there is not a single Mahalanobis "distance" for each person.  If you want to use subclassification I recommend using a propensity-score based distance instead.

I hope this helps.

Liz


